---
# Fetch targets for the Anthology's second view (#1641).
#
# /anthology.html used to ship both panels of the Conference Navigator, about
# 1,000 list rows, at 1,530,626 bytes. The panel a reader is not looking at
# carried data-pagefind-ignore, so it earned nothing where it sat and still
# cost 639,520 bytes of it. archive-page.njk now renders the default view
# only, and archive.js fetches the other from here the first time its tab is
# activated.
#
# One template, six pages: the two views across the three locales. They are
# machine-fetched rather than read, so they carry no site chrome and no
# layout, only the panel div archive.js lifts out and the script tags it
# re-creates (a script inserted as parsed HTML does not execute, so the
# loader rebuilds them).
#
# Excluded from collections, so no sitemap entry and no visual-sitemap row,
# and noindex + data-pagefind-ignore, so neither a crawler nor site search
# treats a bare fragment as a destination. That leaves the by-paper view
# unindexed, which is what shipping it behind data-pagefind-ignore on the
# canonical page already meant.
pagination:
  data: archiveFragments
  size: 1
  alias: frag
permalink: "/fragments/anthology-{{ frag.view }}.{{ frag.lang }}.html"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{%- set lang = frag.lang -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ frag.lang }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ frag.canonical }}">
  <title>{{ frag.view }} · {{ frag.lang }}</title>
</head>
<body data-pagefind-ignore>
<div class="archive-panel" id="archive-panel-{{ frag.view }}" data-archive-panel="{{ frag.view }}">
  {%- if frag.view == "papers" %}
  {% include "papers-page.njk" %}
  {%- else %}
  {% include "speakers-index.njk" %}
  {%- endif %}
</div>
</body>
</html>
